  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Fusion Centre</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment supports Pacific security decision makers through an online portal, enhances information sharing, cooperation, analysis, and assessment, and expands situational awareness and security capability across the Pacific. The Pacific Fusion Centre (the Centre) delivers strategic analysis against security priorities identified by Pacific Islands Forum Leaders in the 2018 Boe Declaration on Regional Security (the Boe Declaration). These priorities include Climate Security, Human Security, Transnational Crime, Cyber Security and Environmental &amp; Resource Security. The Centre&#x2019;s strategic assessments inform Pacific decision-making and strengthen national, sub-regional and regional responses to shared security threats and vulnerabilities. The Centre provides on the job training for analysts. Pacific security officials are hosted at the Centre in Port Vila and engage in training and production of strategic assessments and briefing materials used by national and regional leaders.</narrative>
  </description>
